Z||000000||walsh2001||04-18-2001||09:05 AM||||When I accelerate (in any gear) to above 2500 rpm I hear a weird rattling sound from the engine. It is kind of a mixture between a bee and a mettalic clicking. Car seems to run fine anyway... any ideas?||||reg||11
Z||000001||walsh2001||04-18-2001||09:06 AM||||It is an 84 coupe (manual)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||04-18-2001||09:18 AM||||Loose heat shield?<BR>Check it out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||04-18-2001||09:41 AM||||Heat Shield in the engine bay, Vin plate on the dash, rear view mirror, Sunroof latch just to name a few. where does it sound like its coming from front, back, everywhere? Sometimes you need to poke your head arround and get a good fix on where its coming from. I had a hole in my exhaust once that sounded like a squeek under my seat. My vin plate worked loose once and it sounded like it was coming from behind me. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 04-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||04-18-2001||06:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by walsh2001:<BR><B>When I accelerate (in any gear) to above 2500 rpm I hear a weird rattling sound from the engine. It is kind of a mixture between a bee and a mettalic clicking. Car seems to run fine anyway... any ideas?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I had a cracked piston skirt sound like that...<BR>Till it fell off and tipped the piston in the cylinder...<BR>And it could be failed lifters...<BR>Or low oil pressure at the cam...<BR>Or...||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT GT 87||04-18-2001||07:16 PM||||I have a 87 gt with a rod knock.  It sounds like what you said. Instead of 5w-30 , I run 20w-50 Mobil 1.  When the oil gets hotter , ( not coolant ), you can hear the rod knock more. It is not noticable when I get on it , I think the extra noise drownes it out.                 Steve||||reg||1
Z||000006||jaguiler||04-20-2001||04:24 PM||||I had a hollow cat converter once with a pinhole in it.  The hot exhust would come out and hit the heat shield which made a metallic high pitched rattle.<P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
